  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 408 AM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nA sprawling mid/upper ridge continues to meander over the Southern \nand Central Plains bringing hot and dry weather conditions to the \narea. This feature is progged to translate slowly eastward as we \nmove into the middle of the week before building back over the area \nlate in the week and into the weekend. This is expected to bring a \nprolonged period of hot and dry weather to the area. With persistent \nsoutherly winds through the week, we may gradually begin to see a \nsubtle increase in low-level moisture late Wed into Thu, especially \nacross eastern Kansas, but given the very dry antecedent conditions, \nconfidence remains somewhat low at this time. This could result in \nhigher humidity and an increase in afternoon heat indices as we move \ninto the latter portion of the week and perhaps into the weekend. \nOtherwise dry weather and much above normal temperatures will \nprevail through the upcoming 7 days.",
